From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Svensson <blue@cmd.nu>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:38:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] syncd: don't discover ports after a bulk create that created
 none

When the vendor SAI refuses every port of a bulk create (for example a
breakout mode the ASIC can't do), processBulkOidCreate still called
onPostPortsCreate with zero RIDs. The empty discovery issued HMGET
RIDTOVID without fields, redis rejected it, and the exception put syncd
in shutdown-wait, which took orchagent and the whole data plane down.

Skip the post-create discovery when nothing was created, and make
getVidsForRids return early for an empty list. The per-object statuses
go back to the caller as before.

Refs kamelnetworks/sonic-buildimage#172

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012hdRF8Zy5SCkLbDUZhMxWh
---
 syncd/RedisClient.cpp | 6 ++++++
 syncd/Syncd.cpp       | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/syncd/RedisClient.cpp b/syncd/RedisClient.cpp
index 4f4c4791..7463acbb 100644
--- a/syncd/RedisClient.cpp
+++ b/syncd/RedisClient.cpp
@@ -811,6 +811,12 @@ void RedisClient::getVidsForRids(
 {
     SWSS_LOG_ENTER();
 
+    if (count == 0)
+    {
+        // HMGET needs at least one field
+        return;
+    }
+
     swss::RedisCommand hmget;
 
     std::vector<std::string> cmds;
diff --git a/syncd/Syncd.cpp b/syncd/Syncd.cpp
index 1d127186..f7edc773 100644
--- a/syncd/Syncd.cpp
+++ b/syncd/Syncd.cpp
@@ -3390,7 +3390,13 @@ sai_status_t Syncd::processBulkOidCreate(
 
     m_translator->insertRidsAndVids(createdRids.size(), createdRids.data(), createdVids.data());
 
-    if (objectType == SAI_OBJECT_TYPE_PORT)
+    /*
+     * With every port of the bulk refused by the vendor SAI there is nothing
+     * to discover, and an empty discovery issues HMGET RIDTOVID without
+     * fields, which redis rejects. That exception put syncd in shutdown-wait
+     * and took orchagent down with it; return the statuses instead.
+     */
+    if (objectType == SAI_OBJECT_TYPE_PORT && !createdRids.empty())
     {
         m_switches.at(switchVid)->onPostPortsCreate(createdRids.size(), createdRids.data());
     }
